<h2 id="spaces-pushouts-section-pushouts-II" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="0GG2">81.7</span> Pushouts along closed immersions and integral morphisms</h2>

<p>
This section is analogue of More on Morphisms, Section <a href="/tag/0ECH" data-tag="0ECH">37.67</a>. 
</p>
<p>
<article class="env-lemma" id="0EDP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EDP">Lemma <span data-tag="0EDP">81.7.1</span>.</a> In More on Morphisms, Situation <a href="/tag/0ECI" data-tag="0ECI">37.67.1</a> let $Y \amalg _ Z X$ be the pushout in the category of schemes (More on Morphisms, Proposition <a href="/tag/0E25" data-tag="0E25">37.67.3</a>). Then $Y \amalg _ Z X$ is also a pushout in the category of algebraic spaces over $S$. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a consequence of Lemma <a href="/tag/07SX" data-tag="07SX">81.3.1</a>, the proposition mentioned in the lemma and More on Morphisms, Lemmas <a href="/tag/0ECK" data-tag="0ECK">37.67.6</a> and <a href="/tag/0ECL" data-tag="0ECL">37.67.7</a>. Conditions (1) and (2) of Lemma <a href="/tag/07SX" data-tag="07SX">81.3.1</a> follow immediately. To see (3) and (4) note that an étale morphism is locally quasi-finite and use that the equivalence of categories of More on Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0ECL" data-tag="0ECL">37.67.7</a> is constructed using the pushout construction of More on Morphisms, Lemmas <a href="/tag/0ECK" data-tag="0ECK">37.67.6</a>. Minor details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>
